From af3d78d52f6d3e9f2d0360fd625f5085f370eee2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:15:42 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: Add the S5K3L6 sensor

Some Huawei MateBook E Go units carry an S5K3L6 rear camera (Lijing
module) instead of the OV13B10. Add its camera sensor helper, its sensor
properties and a qcom-ife tuning file.

The helper takes the data pedestal (64 at 10 bits) and the exposure
margin (8 lines, which the kernel driver applies) of the Windows driver's
module configuration, and the analogue gain model gain = code / 32,
which matches the 16x maximum gain of that configuration. The unit cell
size is 1.12 um, the pixel size of that configuration. The control
delays, measured on such a unit, are those of the OV13B10: exposure,
gain and frame length written early in a frame take effect two frames
later.

Awb, Ccm, Abf and Lsc come from the tuning the Windows camera driver
ships for this module; the Lsc grid spans the 4160x3120 full-size
readout, the sensor's default crop rectangle. Agc, Gamma and Bf are
those of the OV13B10, which has the same focal length, f-number and
focus actuator. The sensor corrects its phase detection pixels itself,
so there is no Pdpc.

Tested on an S5K3L6 unit with the camera HAL: 4160x3120 photos with the
display output, 1080p recordings at 30 and 60 fps, and a 1080p stream at
60 fps. The tuning has not been calibrated on such a unit.

Signed-off-by: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
